U(DEV,"optacon2",{s:{cpu:"No processor is named in TSI or museum descriptions. The Optacon II (1985, built with Canon) is described as having a 100-pin tactile array (down from 144) and a computer interface.",ram:"No memory figure is published. The Optacon converts the camera image to the tactile array directly, with no OCR or text storage (HCI Museum).",price:"No Optacon II list price was found. Related figures: an Optacon bought in 1985 for about $3,000 (optacon-l, model not stated); TSI's Optacon price was $4,495 in the 1990s (NFB-RD list)."},src:["https://interfacemuseum.com/exhibits/optacon-ii/","https://www.freelists.org/post/optacon-l/was-Jim-Blisss-death-Now-Buying-Used-Optacons,1","https://nfbcal.org/nfb-rd/0949.html"]});
